# CLI Development

## Overview

The CLI (`create-unstoppable-app`) scaffolds new projects with the Unstoppable Stack. It prompts users for project name and AI assistant, then generates the project with tool-specific agent configurations.

## Key Files

- `packages/cli/src/index.ts` — CLI entry point, Commander.js setup, interactive prompts
- `packages/cli/src/constants.ts` — Assistants definitions
- `packages/cli/src/scaffold.ts` — Project scaffolding logic (generate project, process package.json, install deps)
- `packages/cli/src/agent-pack/index.ts` — Agent pack builder (generates Claude/Cursor/OpenCode configs)
- `packages/cli/agent-pack-src/` — Content bundled with CLI (synced from agent-pack via sync script)

## Build & Test

```bash
cd packages/cli
npx tsup src/index.ts --format esm --dts   # Build
node dist/index.js                           # Run locally
```

## Agent Pack Builder (v2)

The `buildAgentPack()` function in `src/agent-pack/index.ts` loads content from `agent-pack-src/` and generates tool-specific configs:

### Content Loading
- `core/` — Always included
- `modules/` — Only modules selected by user
- `recipes/` — All recipes
- `skills/` — Thin SKILL.md + resources/ (progressive disclosure)
- `hooks/` — skill-rules.json for auto-activation

### Claude Code Output
- Slim `CLAUDE.md` (≤8KB) — overview + available skills list
- `.claude/rules/` — core docs + path-scoped module docs
- `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` + `resources/` — full progressive disclosure
- `.claude/settings.json` — permissions + PostToolUse formatting hook

### Cursor Output
- `project.mdc` (alwaysApply) — slim project overview
- `core-*.mdc` — agent-choice via description
- `module-*.mdc` — glob-scoped to relevant file patterns
- `skill-*.mdc` — description-triggered skill docs
- `p2p-patterns.mdc` / `qvac-patterns.mdc` — glob-scoped pattern rules

### OpenCode Output
- Slim `instructions.md` — overview + available skills/agents
- `opencode.json` — skill gating (only relevant skills enabled)
- `.opencode/agents/` — specialized agents (planner, p2p-expert, ai-expert)
- `.opencode/skills/*/SKILL.md` + `resources/` — full progressive disclosure

## Adding New Skills

1. Create `packages/agent-pack/src/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` (≤4KB)
2. Create `packages/agent-pack/src/skills/<skill-name>/resources/` with deep content
3. Add skill → module mapping in `skillModuleMap` in `src/agent-pack/index.ts`
4. Update `skill-rules.json` with keywords for auto-activation
5. Sync to CLI: `cp -r packages/agent-pack/src/* packages/cli/agent-pack-src/`
6. Rebuild: `cd packages/cli && npx tsup src/index.ts --format esm --dts`
